# Vercel Logging & Monitoring

This project deploys to Vercel with structured JSON logging. Use the Vercel CLI to inspect production behavior.

## Deployment Info

- **Project**: `studious` (org: `liams-projects-659f8cf7`)
- **Production URL**: `studious-beta.vercel.app`
- **Repo**: `LDCODES12/Studious` on GitHub, auto-deploys on push to `main`

## Check Deployment Status

```bash
vercel ls                          # list recent deployments with status
vercel inspect <deployment-url>    # detailed info on a specific deploy
```

## View Logs

```bash
# Recent logs (last hour, expanded with full messages)
vercel logs --no-follow --since 1h --expand

# Stream live logs from a specific deployment
vercel logs <deployment-url>

# Errors only
vercel logs --no-follow --level error --since 1h --expand

# Filter by keyword (e.g. canvas sync, schedule, gradescope)
vercel logs --no-follow --query "sync" --since 1h --expand

# JSON output for piping/parsing
vercel logs --no-follow --json --since 1h

# Filter by HTTP status code
vercel logs --no-follow --status-code 500 --since 6h

# Filter by source type
vercel logs --no-follow --source serverless --since 1h
```

## Logging Architecture

All API routes use `apiLogger()` from `src/lib/logger.ts`. Every log line is structured JSON with fields:

```
{ ts, level, route, userId, duration, status, message, ...extras }
```

Key routes with extensive logging:

- `POST /api/canvas/import` — the main sync endpoint. Logs per-course debug info: syllabus sources with scores, AI extraction attempts (source, format, weeks found, accepted/rejected), audit pass results, class schedule extraction source, material imports. Returns a `debug` object in the response body that the Chrome extension persists to `chrome.storage.local.lastSyncDebug`.
- `POST /api/gradescope/import` — logs matched courses, updated/created assignment counts, cross-source date reconciliation from syllabus events.
- `POST /api/chat` — logs course context and message count.
- `POST /api/syllabus/parse` — logs parsed event counts.
- The Chrome extension also POSTs breadcrumb logs to `POST /api/extension-log` which are persisted in Vercel logs.

## Testing Workflow

The developer tests by deleting all courses in Study Circle, then re-syncing everything via the Chrome extension. This triggers the full `canvas/import` pipeline. Monitor with:

```bash
# Watch the sync in real-time
vercel logs --follow --query "canvas" --expand

# After sync, check for errors
vercel logs --no-follow --level error --since 10m --expand

# See full sync summary
vercel logs --no-follow --query "sync" --since 10m --json | grep "summary"
```

## Slow Query Detection

In development, Prisma logs queries taking >200ms (configured in `src/lib/db.ts`). These appear as `slow_query` entries in stdout.
